<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of Nejd</h1><p class="st-meta">1921 CE – 1926 CE · capital Riyadh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Ibn Saud's state after the conquest of Ha'il, which fixed its northern borders and launched the conquest of the Hejaz.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1921, after taking Ha'il and ending the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-jabal-shammar">Emirate of Jabal Shammar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Abd al-Aziz ibn Saud</a> adopted the title <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Nejd</a> and its Dependencies, replacing the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-nejd-and-hasa">Emirate of Nejd and Hasa</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>, his ally under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-darin">Treaty of Darin</a>, recognised the new title.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sultanate covered central and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and, from 1920, highland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asir">Asir</a>. Its frontiers with the new British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations-mandate">mandates</a> were set at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uqair-protocol">Uqair conference</a> of 1922, which drew the borders with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-kuwait">Sheikhdom of Kuwait</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-iraq">Kingdom of Iraq</a> and created two neutral zones. The Ikhwan raided <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-transjordan">Transjordan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and Kuwait, causing clashes with British forces. In 1924 they attacked the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hejaz">Kingdom of Hejaz</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jeddah">Jeddah</a> fell, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Ibn Saud</a> was proclaimed King of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hejaz">Hejaz</a> in January 1926, joining his two realms as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hejaz-and-nejd">Kingdom of Hejaz and Nejd</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sultanate-of-nejd.jpg" alt="Sultanate of Nejd" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: The Shura Council · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Saudi_Arabia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1921 CE – 1926 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Riyadh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abd al-Aziz ibn Saud</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (Wahhabi)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sultanate of Nejd and its Dependencies</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1924&amp;focus=sultanate-of-nejd" aria-label="Sultanate of Nejd on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5921 1271 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sultanate of Nejd lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6241 1527L6095 1425M6241 1527L6241 1527M6241 1527L4997 651M6241 1527L6241 1527M6241 1527L6070 1642"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6095 1425h0M6241 1527h0M4997 651h0M6241 1527h0M6070 1642h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6241 1527h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6241 1527h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Riyadh. <a href="/atlas?year=1924&amp;focus=sultanate-of-nejd">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
